Short Description:

Onboard Missouri Production Environment to AWS Elastic Disaster Recovery (DRS)

Description:

As part of the Missouri Provider+ Disaster Recovery implementation, please initiate the onboarding of the Missouri Production environment into AWS Elastic Disaster Recovery (DRS).

The objective is to establish AWS DRS protection for the applicable Missouri Production servers and ensure replication is configured to support recovery operations in the designated Missouri DR environment.

Requested Activities:

1. Identify and confirm the Missouri Production EC2 instances requiring AWS DRS protection.
2. Confirm the source AWS account, region, and applicable Production VPC.
3. Configure AWS DRS replication settings in the designated DR account and region using the approved replication subnet.
4. Coordinate installation and configuration of AWS DRS replication agents on the applicable Production servers.
5. Validate network connectivity and required permissions for DRS replication.
6. Verify that all applicable Production servers are successfully registered as DRS source servers and achieve healthy replication status.
7. Configure and validate the recovery launch settings to use the newly provisioned Missouri DR VPC and appropriate recovery subnets.
8. Confirm completion of onboarding and provide the list of protected servers and their replication status.

